{"source_passage_id": "HHS3190M-L03-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0011-PASSAGE", "text": "• Tonicity\n• Ability of a solution to change the shape of cells by altering the cells’ internal water volume\n• Isotonic solution has same tonicity as inside the cell, so volume of cell remains unchanged\n• Hypertonic solution has higher osmolarity than inside cell, so water flows out of cell, resulting in cell shrinking\n• Hypotonic solution has lower osmolarity than inside cell, so water flows into cell, resulting in cell swelling or bursting", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L03-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 3 - Membrane Transport (July 2026)", "source_file": "05 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L3 (Jul 2026).pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS3190M-L03-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0011"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS3190M-L03-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0011", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L03-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 3 - Membrane Transport (July 2026)", "source_file": "05 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L3 (Jul 2026).pdf", "page_number": 11, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 11, "pdf_page": 11, "formatted": "05 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L3 (Jul 2026).pdf, slide 11 (PDF p. 11)"}], "slide_number": 11, "section_ids": ["HHS3190M-L03-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0011", "HHS3190M-L03-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-PART02", "HHS3190M-L03-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "HHS3190M-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS3190M - Human Physiology and Functional Anatomy for Rehabilitation Services", "Lecture 3 - Membrane Transport (July 2026)", "Passive membrane transport", "• Tonicity"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
